The feasibility of predictive selection depends on pre-outcome descriptors of historical relationships and the incumbent's candidate scores. In the 46,878-event Twitch DEV feature-family analysis, combining history and Base-score signals improves selective value over either family alone at a common 6,563 Memory calls (Table~\ref{tab:results-feature-ablation}). This supports the feature-level interpretation of marginal utility without creating another frozen TEST.

